Smoke test for `markdown-backslash-escapes`. Each row's "Live" column should render to match the "Expected" column. If they diverge, the rule is broken or the regex char-class is missing a CommonMark punctuation char.

| Source | Expected | Live |
|---|---|---|
| `\*` | `*` | \* |
| `\_` | `_` | \_ |
| `` \` `` | `` ` `` | \` |
| `\[` | `[` | \[ |
| `\]` | `]` | \] |
| `\(` | `(` | \( |
| `\)` | `)` | \) |
| `\{` | `{` | \{ |
| `\}` | `}` | \} |
| `\<` | `<` | \< |
| `\>` | `>` | \> |
| `\!` | `!` | \! |
| `\#` | `#` | \# |
| `\\` | `\` | \\ |
| `\~` | `~` | \~ |
| `\|` | `\|` | \| |
| `\"` | `"` | \" |
| `\'` | `'` | \' |
| `\$` | `$` | \$ |
| `\%` | `%` | \% |
| `\&` | `&` | \& |
| `\+` | `+` | \+ |
| `\,` | `,` | \, |
| `\-` | `-` | \- |
| `\.` | `.` | \. |
| `\/` | `/` | \/ |
